# portfolioBacktest/cache — 2.4GB of M1/H1/H4/D1 parquet, refreshed by copying new
# files in. It was half-managed: 12 _m1 files ignored by name, 10 others TRACKED,
# and a data refresh left 128 more untracked — so `git add -A` would have staged
# most of 2.4GB into a repo that pushes to GitHub. Ignore the directory instead of
# chasing filenames, which drifts every time the cache gains a pair or a timeframe.
# The tracked ones were removed with `git rm --cached`; they remain on disk.
portfolioBacktest/cache/

# CVOL history: the copy in data/cvol/ is the one forge reads (see forge/vol.py).
